{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-j2-reviewer-fable-46","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:9fa78aaf352649e179f8","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The workflow collapses each tank's repeated overnight sessions into a single tank-level mean before any statistical procedure runs: collapse_to_tanks groups session MO2 values by tank_id and stores one mean per tank.","observed_value":"12 tank means produced from 46 session rows","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":40,"end_line":40,"quoted_text":"\"\"\"Average the repeated sessions of a tank into a single tank-level value.\"\"\""},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":45,"end_line":45,"quoted_text":"readings.setdefault(tank_id, []).append(mo2)"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":54,"end_line":54,"quoted_text":"\"mean_mo2\": float(np.mean(values)),"}]},{"description":"The Mann-Whitney U test is applied only to tank-level values: group_means extracts one mean_mo2 per tank per diet, and stats.mannwhitneyu receives those two arrays of six tank means each; the 46 session rows never enter the test.","observed_value":"mannwhitneyu on 6 vs 6 tank means","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":62,"end_line":63,"quoted_text":"return np.array(\n        [tank[\"mean_mo2\"] for tank in tanks if tank[\"diet\"] == diet], dtype=float"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":74,"end_line":76,"quoted_text":"test = stats.mannwhitneyu(\n        supplemented, control, alternative=\"two-sided\", method=\"exact\"\n    )"}]},{"description":"The reported statistics are consistent with a test on 12 tank means, not 46 rows. Recomputing by hand from the CSV: control tank means 209.75, 198.20, 219.30, 205.10, 215.60, 202.45 and beta-glucan means 228.75, 212.30, 241.25, 224.40, 233.10, 237.90 give U = 34 (beta-glucan vs control), exact two-sided p = 8/924 = 0.008658, rank-biserial 2*34/36 - 1 = 0.889, and group means 208.40 vs 229.62 — all matching the report exactly.","observed_value":"U=34.0, p=0.008658, rank-biserial 0.889 reproduced from 6 vs 6 tank means","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":41,"end_line":42,"quoted_text":"The exact Mann-Whitney U test on the 12 tank means gives U = 34.0,\np = 0.008658, rank-biserial correlation 0.889."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":44,"end_line":44,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Tanks fed the beta-glucan supplement had higher routine oxygen uptake than control tanks (two-sided exact Mann-Whitney U on 6 vs 6 tank means, U = 34.0, p = 0.008658, rank-biserial 0.889)."}]},{"description":"The report's stated analysis matches the code and the data description's requirement to summarise within tank before comparing diets, and it explicitly claims session rows were never entered into the test.","observed_value":"report analysis section consistent with workflow","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":14,"end_line":18,"quoted_text":"Sessions were averaged within each tank before any test was run, so every tank\ncontributes exactly one value (mass-specific oxygen uptake, MO2, in mg O2 kg^-1 h^-1) to\nthe comparison. The two diets were then compared with a two-sided exact Mann-Whitney U\ntest on the 12 tank means (6 control vs 6 beta-glucan). The individual session rows were\nnever entered into the test."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":27,"end_line":28,"quoted_text":"available for any diet comparison. Session values should therefore be summarised within a\ntank before a between-diet comparison is made."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The precondition for the issue class is present in the data: the same independent unit (tank_id) appears on multiple rows, 46 sessions from only 12 tanks, so a row-level analysis would have constituted pseudoreplication had the workflow used the rows directly. This is the structure that had to be checked against the code path.","observed_value":"46 rows from 12 tanks (T05 and T10 have 3 sessions, all others 4)","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":25,"end_line":26,"quoted_text":"Because the same tank appears on several rows, the rows are repeated measurements of the\nsame unit: the 46 rows come from only 12 tanks"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":14,"quoted_text":"T01,control,1,12.1,24,205.6\nT02,bglucan,1,12.1,24,224.6\nT03,control,1,12.0,24,194.5\nT04,bglucan,1,12.2,23,208.7\nT05,control,1,12.1,24,216.4\nT06,bglucan,1,12.0,24,236.8\nT07,control,1,12.2,23,200.7\nT08,bglucan,1,12.1,24,220.3\nT09,control,1,12.0,24,211.8\nT10,bglucan,1,12.2,24,229.8\nT11,control,1,12.1,24,198.6\nT12,bglucan,1,12.1,23,233.5\nT01,control,2,12.4,24,211.2"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to show that repeated tank rows enter the row-independent test despite the report's claim. Traced the full data path: read_sessions yields 46 session tuples, collapse_to_tanks reduces them to 12 tank dictionaries keyed by tank_id, group_means selects only the single mean_mo2 per tank, and mannwhitneyu receives exactly those 6-element arrays; no other code path passes session-level values to any test. I then recomputed the tank means from the CSV (verifying T01 = 209.75, T05 = 657.9/3 = 219.30, T10 = 699.3/3 = 233.10, etc.), derived U = 34 by counting cross-group pairs, and computed the exact two-sided p as 8/924 = 0.008658 and rank-biserial 0.889 — identical to the reported values. A row-level test on 25 vs 21 sessions would have produced a much larger U and a different p, so the reported numbers are only reproducible from the collapsed tank means. The falsification attempt failed; the sample size claimed and used is one value per independent unit.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}